# oc-prune configuration – copy to .env (gitignored) and adjust.
# Environment variables take precedence over the values set here.
#
# BACKUP gets both the exports of deleted sessions (subdirectories per
# project) and, with --vacuum, a full copy of the database:
#   $BACKUP/opencode-20261014-221530.db
# The directory must already exist – the script will not create it.
#
# BACKUP=$HOME/opencode-export
#
# Optional: with --vacuum the full database copy is uploaded to this SSH target
# instead of BACKUP (no local temporary copy). Format: [user@]host:/absolute/path
# Requires passwordless SSH, rsync and sha256sum on the remote; the directory
# must already exist. Exports of deleted sessions still go to BACKUP.
#BACKUP_REMOTE=user@host:/path/to/backup
# ROOT=$HOME/projects
# DAYS=30
# MIN=3
# ONLY=/path/to/a/single/project
# DB=$HOME/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db
# SIZES=1
